==========================================================================
Sales-Connections - Alembic Database Migrations
==========================================================================

This folder contains all Alembic 1.x migration scripts that bring a
fresh PostgreSQL 17.7 database to the schema required by the
Sales-Connections backend (per AAP Sec 0.4.7).

For the canonical migration runbook (deploy procedure, rollback,
secret rotation, dual-role separation), see:

    docs/operations.md - "Migrations" section
    docs/architecture.md - "Data Tier" section


Quick Reference (run from the backend/ directory)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Generate a new migration via autogenerate (compares app.models with
   the live database schema):

       alembic revision --autogenerate -m "short_slug_describing_change"

2. Apply all pending migrations:

       alembic upgrade head

3. Roll back the most recent migration:

       alembic downgrade -1

4. Show the current head and history:

       alembic current
       alembic history --verbose

5. Stamp the database to a specific revision without running migrations
   (only use when recovering from a broken migration state):

       alembic stamp <revision_id>


Coordination Points
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  - Models registered on db.metadata are imported by env.py from
    app.models (via the package __init__.py re-exports).

  - Database URL is read from the current Flask config (created by
    app.create_app()), which itself sources DATABASE_URL from the
    environment or AWS Secrets Manager.

  - The Dockerfile invokes 'alembic upgrade head' at container startup
    when the RUN_MIGRATIONS environment variable is set to 'true'.

  - The application role used at runtime has INSERT-only privileges on
    the audit_events table; a separate elevated migrations role retains
    full DDL/DML privileges. See the GRANT/REVOKE block in the initial
    schema migration.


File Naming Convention
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Migrations are numbered sequentially with a zero-padded prefix:

    0001_initial_schema.py
    0002_add_<feature>.py
    0003_add_<feature>.py

Each migration has a descriptive slug after the number. Down-revision
chains are linear (no branching) for MVP simplicity.


